# An imported extension's Web Store install downloads its CRX through Chrome's downloads. Since engine -18 Cra keeps
# it out of its own lists and guards (web-store-install-quit-guards), but Chromium's badge on the Dock tile still
# counted every download in progress: on 0.1.50 the first page of each launch put a download on Cra's Dock icon that
# no list showed (GitHub #491, 19 Nov 2026). Here the store sends 64 KB of the CRX and then nothing, so the install
# is still downloading when the badge is read. A download the person starts next is on the badge, alone: the
# readout's count is real, and the install's download is still not in it.
# promise: #491
home
budget rss=600
extension ${FIXTURES}/WebStoreCopy/${WEB_STORE_COPY_ID}
arg --apps-gallery-download-url=${TRICKLE}/%s.crx
cra://open?url=${PAGE}?n=store
expect-log extension ${WEB_STORE_COPY_ID}: installing from the Web Store in Default
wait 3
reject-log Web Store install in Default failed
cra://debug?dockTile=installing
expect-log dock tile installing: .*downloads=0$
cra://open?url=${TRICKLE}/trickle.bin
wait 2
cra://debug?downloadState=started
expect-log download state started: running=true
cra://debug?dockTile=downloading
expect-log dock tile downloading: view=DockTileView .*downloads=1$
cra://debug?download=cancel
expect-log download control: cancel
wait 1
